---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Projects - Kris Kemper">
  <h2>Projects</h2>

  <section class="project">
    <h3>Partwright</h3>
    <p>
      A browser-based parametric CAD tool designed for
      AI-driven 3D modeling. Describe something, get a
      printable 3D model. No backend, no installs. Built on
      <a href="https://github.com/elalish/manifold">manifold-3d</a>
      for fast WASM boolean operations, Three.js for
      rendering, and CodeMirror for the editor.
    </p>
    <p>
      The key idea is a <code>window.partwright</code>
      console API that lets AI agents create, validate,
      and iterate on designs programmatically. You can
      save multiple design variations and compare them
      in a gallery view, which is useful for AI
      workflows that generate N variations for human
      review. Works best with the
      <a href="https://claude.ai/download">Claude Chrome extension</a>.
    </p>
    <p><a href="https://www.partwrightstudio.com/">Launch Partwright &gt;</a></p>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <section class="project">
    <h3>openscad_projects</h3>
    <p>
      3D models designed entirely by AI using OpenSCAD,
      a programmatic CAD tool. Functional designs meant
      for 3D printing. The kind of hands-on fabrication
      work that eventually led me to build Partwright.
    </p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/kemper/openscad_projects">View source &gt;</a></p>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .project {
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }

  .project h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.8em;
  }

</style>
